 "findings": [
  {
   "file": "plugins/specclaw/tests/run-infosec-evals.sh",
   "fp": "e0621c301093",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 117,
   "message": "The eval runner has its own BLOCK-heading parser, and it disagrees with the gate's. The catch check uses `^### \\[(BLOCK|WARN|NOTE)\\]` and the false-alarm check uses `^### \\[BLOCK\\]`. Both match only an uppercase, bracketed, level-3 tag at column 0. specclaw-security-gate's BLOCK_HEADING also accepts `##`\u2013`######`, any case, emoji or list-number prefixes and a bare `BLOCK`, so the nightly false-alarm rate does not measure what actually blocks a PR. Share one heading definition: let the runner call the gate on the report, or export the regex. Alternatively, mirror BLOCK_HEADING and add a stub row that emits an emoji-prefixed BLOCK.",
   "original_severity": "major",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "B4",
   "scenario": "The model reviews a fixed sample and prints `### \ud83d\udd34 [BLOCK] src/handler.js:2 \u2014 B16 DevFlags`. specclaw-security-gate exits 1 on this report and stops the PR. The runner's `^### \\[BLOCK\\]` does not match, so the result says `False-alarm rate: 0%`.",
   "severity": "major"
  },
  {
   "file": "plugins/specclaw-review/tests/run-review-tests.sh",
   "fp": "f811df210c0a",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 575,
   "message": "The 'every security rule is present' guards list only the first batch of rules. The fix-round additions are missing. sec_ids lacks B21 B22 B23 B24 (base), DN10 DN11 (dotnet) and PY12 PY13 (python). In run-preset-check-tests.sh, the security_missing default keys lack Config, Identity and Redirects, and stack_keys lacks RateLimit and Proxy for dotnet and python. A rule from that batch can be deleted and these suites stay green. Add every id and keyword that the packs and presets in this diff define. Better, derive the expected list once instead of keeping a hand copy.",
   "original_severity": "major",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "B1",
   "scenario": "Delete the `- **DN10** ...` line from review-rules/dotnet.md, or the `- **Proxy:**` line from presets/python.md. run-review-tests.sh and run-preset-check-tests.sh both still pass. DN10 has no eval case either, so nothing in CI fails.",
   "severity": "major"
  },
  {
   "file": "plugins/specclaw/bin/specclaw-pr",
   "fp": "caab02715aca",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 471,
   "message": "`specclaw-security-gate --waivers 2>/dev/null || true`, together with a silent skip when the gate is not executable, makes 'could not list waivers' read the same as 'no waivers'. The PR body then just omits the section. Surface a failed listing, for example a warn or a `## Security waivers` line saying the waiver list could not be read.",
   "original_severity": "minor",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "B3",
   "scenario": "",
   "severity": "minor"
  },
  {
   "file": "plugins/specclaw/bin/specclaw-build-context",
   "fp": "b33db454f24f",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 288,
   "message": "When specclaw-presets prints a path that is not a file, `[[ -f \"$preset_path\" ]] || continue` drops it with no warning. The builder then silently loses that preset's security rules. Warn on an unreadable resolved path, the same way the resolver-failure branches already do.",
   "original_severity": "minor",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "B3",
   "scenario": "",
   "severity": "minor"
  },
  {
   "file": "plugins/specclaw/tests/run-infosec-evals.sh",
   "fp": "95e9ae3a94b7",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 66,
   "message": "`RULES` is computed from base and node files and never used, because review() uses rules_for per sample. The comment says these are the rules given in a real run, which is misleading. Remove the variable.",
   "original_severity": "minor",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "B10",
   "scenario": "",
   "severity": "minor"
  },
  {
   "file": "plugins/specclaw/bin/specclaw-security-gate",
   "fp": "834502a8d342",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 41,
   "message": "norm_path lowercases every path. On a case-sensitive filesystem, a waiver for one file therefore lifts a BLOCK on a different file whose name differs only in case. Compare case-insensitively only for drive-letter or backslash paths, or not at all.",
   "original_severity": "minor",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "B1",
   "scenario": "",
   "severity": "minor"
  },
  {
   "file": "plugins/specclaw/bin/specclaw-security-gate",
   "fp": "6df45e1d5669",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 54,
   "message": "Any text after the verdict word makes the verdict invalid. A line like `**Verdict:** APPROVED_WITH_NOTES (2 WARN)` becomes `APPROVED_WITH_NOTES_(2_WARN)`, and the gate reports 'security review did not run' (exit 3) for a review that did run. This fails closed, but the message is wrong. Take the first token, or report 'unreadable verdict' separately from 'no report'.",
   "original_severity": "minor",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "B6",
   "scenario": "",
   "severity": "minor"
  }
